  "body": "Normally pairing with my BLE device works fine.\n\nAfter connecting, once I try to subscribe to a characteristic that is protected, the electron pairing handler is called in the main process and allows me to confirm the pairing. This works 100% fine in my case.\n\nBut now, when I delete the bond information from windows (central) and keep it on the peripheral (asymmetric state), subscribing to the characteristic fails with `GATT Error: Not paired.` It does not trigger the pairing handler, which it should.\n\nInterestingly this does not happen, when I try to connect using Windows System Settings. Here connecting works fine, a new pairing is automatically initiated.",
